WEBVTT

00:00.600 --> 00:03.790
This series takes a closer look at each part of HASTE.

00:04.240 --> 00:07.700
In this episode: editing predictions where you review the

00:07.720 --> 00:10.990
model's damage map, and correct it before you share it.

00:15.000 --> 00:17.360
No model is perfect, so before you

00:17.380 --> 00:19.930
share a damage map, it pays to check it.

00:20.360 --> 00:21.960
We open the results of the embedding

00:21.980 --> 00:24.390
model from episode two and click Edit.

00:31.647 --> 00:33.757
The edit panel counts every class:

00:34.007 --> 00:37.637
480 damaged and 1,581 not damaged.

00:38.307 --> 00:40.587
This model gives each building a hard label,

00:40.607 --> 00:42.557
so there's no threshold to tune.

00:42.787 --> 00:44.437
We fix mistakes by hand.

00:45.167 --> 00:48.137
To fix a building, choose a class, and click it.

00:48.687 --> 00:51.107
These five homes survived, but the model flagged

00:51.127 --> 00:53.877
them as damaged, so we mark them Not Damaged.

00:54.637 --> 00:56.397
Each edit gets a blue outline and

00:56.417 --> 00:58.527
stays a local preview until you save.

00:59.327 --> 01:01.177
A few streets away, the opposite,

01:01.567 --> 01:03.537
six burned homes the model missed.

01:04.027 --> 01:05.177
We mark them Damaged.

01:12.100 --> 01:14.260
For a whole row, hold Control and

01:14.280 --> 01:16.330
drag a box to paint them all Damaged.

01:18.407 --> 01:20.747
To double check the rest, we filter the review

01:20.767 --> 01:23.437
to damaged and step through with the arrow keys.

01:24.413 --> 01:27.163
Press 1 for Damaged, or 2 for Not Damaged.

01:32.313 --> 01:34.123
Two more false alarms, fixed.

01:35.333 --> 01:37.543
16 buildings changed in all.

01:37.983 --> 01:39.653
We click Save as new version.

01:41.097 --> 01:44.387
Each save adds a new version, and earlier versions are kept.

01:51.907 --> 01:54.297
The raw model output stays untouched,

01:54.467 --> 01:56.697
so you can switch between the two to compare.

02:03.310 --> 02:06.220
And the edited version downloads as a GeoPackage.

02:06.880 --> 02:09.330
Later in the series, we'll dig into these outputs.

02:10.633 --> 02:14.003
HASTE is open source under the MIT license.

02:14.473 --> 02:17.583
Deploy it to Azure with a single azd up command,

02:17.673 --> 02:19.883
or run it locally with Docker Compose.

02:20.333 --> 02:23.263
Find it on GitHub at microsoft/haste.
